Alex G: Quick sync — planning to bump the JS SDK from 12.x -> 14.1 later today. We use streaming (chat completions), token-rotation hooks, and a custom retry middleware. Anyone run this upgrade already? Any breaking gotchas to call out before I open the PR?

Priya S: Heads-up: auth hook signature changed in 13.x. Old pattern: `onAuth(token, cb)` -> new is async `async function getToken()` that returns `{ token, expiry }`. If you rely on the callback style you'll need a thin adapter.

Dan R: Also, streaming API surface changed: `createStream()` used to return an EventEmitter; now it returns an AsyncIterable of chunks. Most apps will be fine, but if you listen for `'end'`/`'error'` events you need to switch to `for await (const chunk of stream)` or wrap it.

Margo L: Retry defaults were tightened — backoff switched to exponential with capped max delay. If your middleware assumes short fast retries (0.5s) you might see longer first retry. You can opt back to the old profile via `client.config.retries.profile = 'legacy'` for a safe rollout.

Dan R: Small example adapter for streaming -> emitter:```js
// backward compat helper
function streamToEmitter(asyncIter) {
  const ee = new (require('events'))();
  (async () => {
    try {
      for await (const c of asyncIter) ee.emit('data', c);
      ee.emit('end');
    } catch (e) { ee.emit('error', e); }
  })();
  return ee;
}
```

Alex G: Nice, thanks. The token change is the one I'm worried about — we use an in-memory rotating token provider that called the cb. Any quick adapter guidance?

Priya S: Adapter is easy:```js
// old provider: function onAuth(cb) { cb(null, token); }
// adapter: async function getToken() {
//   return new Promise((res, rej) => onAuth((err, t) => err ? rej(err) : res({ token: t })));
// }
```

Jin K: FYI — there was an edge case with streaming metadata: chunk objects used to be `{ text }`, now they include `{ text, meta }`. If you do `Object.assign` into a string buffer you'll need to pull `chunk.text` explicitly. Broke one of our wrappers in staging.

